  "result": "{\"seen_before\": false, \"matches\": [], \"answer\": \"I couldn't find a past ticket reporting this same problem: a cyclic remap of the apostrophe, grave, and backslash keys on a remote US keyboard in Mouse Without Borders. The closest tickets are different problems. PowerToys#40494 describes a key-sequence corruption that affects every key and appears after days of use. PowerToys#45149 is about NumLock state sync. Neither one matches this report, so this looks like a new bug. Please keep the ticket open and include the bug report ZIP. It would help to say whether the remapping persists after restarting Mouse Without Borders on both machines. Also check whether it changes if you switch the remote's input language away from and back to English (US), or remove the Simplified Chinese keyboard, since a layout mismatch on the remote may be involved.\"}",
